Oct25:  Dear Bw,

Thanks for your nice Makefile.
I really like your target "run-%" which I did not know about!

I want to change a few things.  The main thing is that
I want to make the number of input variables
to be INDEPENDENT of the dimension n.  Here are the changes:

(1) If n=2, then
	var ?= x, y
	ff  ?= 2*x-2*x*y,  -y+x*y

	(i.e., var and ff are n-vectors, comma separated)

	NOTE: I want the "comma" separated list because
	it is easier to understand for humans.
	I note that you later convert a comma-separated
	list into a "space" separated list. 
	
	There is probably a Makefile function to do this directly
	(just specify that it is "comma-separated").

(2) I want initial box to be written in the centered form:
	Instead of 
			lo1 ?= 0.9
			hi1 ?= 1.1
			lo2 ?= 2.9
			hi2 ?= 3.1
	I want
		cen ?= 1.0, 3.0
		wid ?= 0.1, 0.1

(3) Similarly, I want outputs to be in centered form.
		Also, wid can be a single number, say 0.1.
		In that case it is an n-vector of all 0.1.

(4) Each of the inputfiles in examples should
	be given meaningful names!  Call them
		egVolterra.mk
		egAlso, every inputfile
	must have some comments!!! 

	I have started doing this for input1.mk,
	which I renamed to egVolterra.mk.
	Please look at the restructure.

	The ONLY requiree information we want these files
		are the INPUT/OUTPUT information for radicalIVP!!!
		EVERYTHING ELSE should be optional.




